  - m_Id: 94000000000000001
    m_Localized: Halvar
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000002
    m_Localized: Elina
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000004
    m_Localized: Orren
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000005
    m_Localized: Marta Veyn
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000006
    m_Localized: Edric
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000007
    m_Localized: Runa
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000008
    m_Localized: Tarek
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000009
    m_Localized: Livio Aguilar
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 40000000000000003
    m_Localized: District Residents
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 40000000000000004
    m_Localized: Mages
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000010
    m_Localized: Erdan Vell
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000011
    m_Localized: Father Cadmon
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000012
    m_Localized: Meyra
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000013
    m_Localized: Harn
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000014
    m_Localized: Garven
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000015
    m_Localized: Lissa
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000016
    m_Localized: Varna
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000017
    m_Localized: Rogan
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000018
    m_Localized: Selm
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000019
    m_Localized: Hedda Roun
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000020
    m_Localized: Corvin Veyr
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000021
    m_Localized: Ulrik
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000022
    m_Localized: Keld Rook
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000023
    m_Localized: Bram Voss
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 94000000000000024
    m_Localized: Varek Holt
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000001
    m_Localized: "Hold. The road feeds us: fifteen gold and you walk where you please. Pay once, and we do not shake you down twice."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000002
    m_Localized: "Here. Fifteen gold."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000003
    m_Localized: "I won't pay robbers for a road."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000004
    m_Localized: "I'd rather cut you and your friends down than pay."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000005
    m_Localized: "Good. Coin goes to the common purse, you go down the road. Do not linger here."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000006
    m_Localized: "Then turn around. You do not want it easy, you can wander the woods."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000007
    m_Localized: "You stepped in it yourself. Boys, show the guest why it is too late to bargain with a knife drawn."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000008
    m_Localized: "About the forest and your people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000009
    m_Localized: "The forest? Forget the trails. Ask the rest while I am feeling kind."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000010
    m_Localized: "About the road payment"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000011
    m_Localized: "What do you want, traveller?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000012
    m_Localized: "All right, something else."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000013
    m_Localized: "Go on. Do not skulk around here."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000014
    m_Localized: "What is this camp deeper in the forest?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000015
    m_Localized: "The camp is beyond the stream. They put strangers in their place quickly there. We were set here to feed off the road; travellers fill the common purse steadier than hunting."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000016
    m_Localized: "Does your chief keep you on a short leash?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000017
    m_Localized: "The chief hates empty hands. The order is simple: squeeze travellers, keep the noise down. A share goes up, crumbs stay with us. That is how we live."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000018
    m_Localized: "And the guard tolerates this?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000019
    m_Localized: "The guard? They used to chase us through every bush: light a fire at night, find spears in the brush by dawn. Now they can barely hold their gates. They have no hands for the forest, so we breathe easier."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000020
    m_Localized: "You think the forest is yours now?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000021
    m_Localized: "The forest belongs to nobody until somebody holds it. First the road, then the trails, then people grow used to asking leave from those with iron. It takes time."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000022
    m_Localized: "So? You opening that purse or not?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000023
    m_Localized: "Here are fifteen gold."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000024
    m_Localized: "I've thought it over. It is cheaper to cut you and your friends down than to pay."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000025
    m_Localized: "Never mind. Forget it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000026
    m_Localized: "Aren't you afraid of the creatures in the forest?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000027
    m_Localized: "I am afraid. Only a fool says otherwise. We keep to the trail, keep the fire alive, and never slip into the thicket alone. A man crawled back from the far post last week: barefoot, no partner. Said, “It walked beside us.” That was all. Even the loudest mouths stopped joking at night."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000028
    m_Localized: "What do you know about the village by the road?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000029
    m_Localized: "The village crouches in its huts waiting for the road to feed it again. The bold hide food. The clever keep their mouths shut. We do not pass by either kind."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000030
    m_Localized: "What are you sniffing around for?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000031
    m_Localized: "What have you done to the mill?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000032
    m_Localized: "We took what stood without an owner. The wheel turns, flour comes out. Anyone needing grain ground leaves coin and keeps clever talk to himself."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000033
    m_Localized: "Where is the miller?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000034
    m_Localized: "Your Ulrik is alive. He sits locked in the mill and gets bread and water. Stays quiet, he sees morning."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000035
    m_Localized: "So you are holding a man hostage."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000036
    m_Localized: "Hostage, captive — words for folk with full bellies. He sits quiet, does not run for the woods or call the guard. Less trouble for us."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000037
    m_Localized: "And the field?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000038
    m_Localized: "We hold the field, the field feeds us. Flour close by, fresh food too. Nobody runs back to camp for every crust. You would not turn your nose up at it either."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000039
    m_Localized: "All right. Let us talk about something else."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 95000000000000040
    m_Localized: "Goodbye."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000001
    m_Localized: "Tell About the Miller's Fate"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000002
    m_Localized: "The miller is held in the mill by bandits. The news needs to reach someone able to act."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000003
    m_Localized: "Ask about the miller"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000004
    m_Localized: "Possible help for the captive miller must be found."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000005
    m_Localized: "Ask at the tavern"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000006
    m_Localized: "The blacksmith suggests looking for help among Halvar's people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000007
    m_Localized: "Tell the guard captain"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000008
    m_Localized: "Halvar believes the city guard must deal with the bandits."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000009
    m_Localized: "Meet the squad at the mill"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000010
    m_Localized: "A guard squad waits at the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000011
    m_Localized: "Help retake the mill"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000012
    m_Localized: "The squad is moving on the bandits. Choose whose side you are on."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000013
    m_Localized: "Report on the miller"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000014
    m_Localized: "The guard captain must learn that bandits hold the miller."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000015
    m_Localized: "Reach the squad at the mill"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000016
    m_Localized: "The guard gathers at the mill before the sortie."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000017
    m_Localized: "Help retake the mill"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 96000000000000018
    m_Localized: "The squad is fighting the bandits at the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000001
    m_Localized: "The miller is being held by bandits. Where can I find help?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000002
    m_Localized: "A bad business. I have a hammer for iron, not a squad for bandits. Ask at Halvar's tavern; people loosen their tongues there."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000003
    m_Localized: "If you need warmth, ale, or a quiet corner, you came to the right counter."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000004
    m_Localized: "Do you know anything about the miller held at the mill?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000005
    m_Localized: "My guests have excuses, not courage. A hostage and armed bandits are the city guard's business. Speak to their captain."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000006
    m_Localized: "The bandits at the mill hold Ulrik hostage."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000007
    m_Localized: "Then we stop waiting. I have sent a squad to the mill; meet them there and keep clear until the order is given."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000008
    m_Localized: "Are you the one we were told to wait for? Aldren Vael, city guard. I hear you ran into bandits at the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000009
    m_Localized: "I am ready. Lead on."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000010
    m_Localized: "The mill is ours again."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000011
    m_Localized: "About the reward."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000012
    m_Localized: "You stood with us when it mattered. Take two healing draughts and a mug of ale. We should drink to those who made it home."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000013
    m_Localized: "What about my share?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000014
    m_Localized: "You watched while others bled. The mill is free; that is your share."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000017
    m_Localized: "I fought with your people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000018
    m_Localized: "Steel spoke and you stood with us. Take the beer and draught. Bram will enjoy hearing how the guard bared its teeth, then dug the ground with them."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000019
    m_Localized: "The guard could not break you."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000020
    m_Localized: "The guard came in howling and left without a word. You stayed out of it — take the beer, and remember whose mill this is."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000021
    m_Localized: "Varek sent me after the mill fight."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000022
    m_Localized: "Varek says you did not flinch when the guard pushed in. That earns you one hundred and fifty coins. Spend them quick, before someone notices your purse is too heavy."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000023
    m_Localized: "You gave me back more than a mill. When the fields are green again, there will be bread for anyone who needs it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000024
    m_Localized: "What is it?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000025
    m_Localized: "Will you help the miller held by bandits?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000026
    m_Localized: "I have children to feed. I am not trading their supper for a stranger's mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000027
    m_Localized: "I saw men with blades once. That was enough for one lifetime."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000028
    m_Localized: "I pay my taxes. Let the people paid to carry swords handle it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000029
    m_Localized: "Do you know anything about the miller?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000030
    m_Localized: "No. And I have no intention of making a bandit's hostage my affair. Take that burden to someone who carries a badge."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000031
    m_Localized: "What would it take for you to release the prisoner?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000032
    m_Localized: "The captive is not on my neck. Bram keeps the keys and the tally, up at the forest camp. Take your purse there; without coin, he will not even look at the man in his lockup."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000033
    m_Localized: "Varek said Bram Voss handles talk about the prisoner."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000034
    m_Localized: "Ah, you came for the man in the lockup. Two thousand coins and Ulrik gets to breathe free. Do not pull a face; freedom is dear merchandise these days."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000035
    m_Localized: "Hand over two thousand coins."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000036
    m_Localized: "Two thousand rang out. Fine. But while you carried them, the tally grew. Another five hundred, and the key turns."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000037
    m_Localized: "Hand over another five hundred coins."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000038
    m_Localized: "Now the account is shut. My people leave the mill. Run and see before I remember that air has a price too."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000039
    m_Localized: "Bram took two thousand for the prisoner and demanded another five hundred."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000040
    m_Localized: "Two thousand, and you expected Bram's word to be honest? An expensive lesson, but you are breathing. My people are already at the mill; meet them and we will drive that gang out by the book."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000041
    m_Localized: "Hello."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 97000000000000042
    m_Localized: "Goodbye."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000003
    m_Localized: "The assault has failed"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000004
    m_Localized: "The guards are dead. Report the failure to the guard captain or try to negotiate with the bandits to free the miller."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000005
    m_Localized: "The squad at the mill is dead."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000006
    m_Localized: "I have no more people. I will not send those left at the gate into the same grave. If you want the miller out, find a way yourself."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000007
    m_Localized: "Ask. Just do not expect me to find my tongue at once. After listening so long for a bolt to scrape, ordinary questions take their time reaching me."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000008
    m_Localized: "There are a few things I would like to ask."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000009
    m_Localized: "What will become of the mill now?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000010
    m_Localized: "First I sweep the straw from beneath the stones. Then I pull the boards off the windows — they nailed them up as if light could be fought. The wheel is sound, the stones are sound. The people's trust, I do not know."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000011
    m_Localized: "Will people come back?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000012
    m_Localized: "When they see smoke from the chimney and hear the wheel, they will. Not for me — for their sacks. Hunger does not ask who held the keys while the mill stood still."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000013
    m_Localized: "Can you manage alone?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000014
    m_Localized: "I can. I know how to hear a stone: when it sings true, when it asks for water, when it is ready to crack. People are harder. A stone, at least, does not lie that it will be back soon."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000015
    m_Localized: "Why does this mill matter so much?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000016
    m_Localized: "While the wheel hums, a field becomes a sack by the door, flour on a palm, a flatbread in a stranger's house. When it falls silent, everyone learns that. Too quickly."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000017
    m_Localized: "So you feed the whole district?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000018
    m_Localized: "No. I only make grain do what it was grown for. The ones who sowed in the cold, hauled the sacks and shared the last crust feed people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000019
    m_Localized: "And what is in it for you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000020
    m_Localized: "My share keeps the roof from leaking and the table from standing bare. I will not pretend sainthood. But I will not inspect a hungry person's clothes before I grind their last sack."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000021
    m_Localized: "What did the bandits do to you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000022
    m_Localized: "First they asked where I kept the silver. I told them silver is not ground from flour. Then they told me to sit quietly. They argued over who would have my work, as if I was already gone."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000023
    m_Localized: "Did they beat you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000024
    m_Localized: "Once, so the others would see. After that they had no need. A person learns to flinch at footsteps quicker than at pain."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000025
    m_Localized: "Why did you not fight back?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000026
    m_Localized: "Because I am a miller. My hands know flour and an old rope knife, not a blade. Burning a mill is easy. Then a hero remains a hero, and people have nothing to eat."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000027
    m_Localized: "What do you think of the guard?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000028
    m_Localized: "Men in mail are still men. Orders, distance and fear slow them while trouble belongs to someone else. I will neither weave them wreaths nor spit after them."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000029
    m_Localized: "They came too late."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000030
    m_Localized: "Too late is when you can answer no one. I can answer. So there is still time."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000031
    m_Localized: "You still owe them."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000032
    m_Localized: "I owe those who opened the door. No more and no less. A debt does not make a person holy, and gratitude does not make me forget."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000033
    m_Localized: "What is the strangest thing you have seen here?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000034
    m_Localized: "Before the bandits, there were three nights. The water was low and something knocked beneath the race: three blows, a pause, then three more. By morning there were fine fish scales on dry stones."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000035
    m_Localized: "Sounds like water or an animal."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000036
    m_Localized: "Perhaps. I have listened to water for twenty years. It does not knock as though waiting for an answer."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000037
    m_Localized: "Why did you tell no one?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000038
    m_Localized: "I meant to understand it first. I did not get the chance. If you hear it again, do not enter the water at night. Call for me."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000039
    m_Localized: "That is enough for now."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000040
    m_Localized: "People are harder than sacks."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000041
    m_Localized: "That is it. A sack needs a dry place. A frightened person may walk past for a year. I will open the door and light the stove; they can decide the rest."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000042
    m_Localized: "You still need people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000043
    m_Localized: "Who does not? A mill without people is a shed with costly stones."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000044
    m_Localized: "You still charge them."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000045
    m_Localized: "I do. But when a widow brings her last sack, I do not strip her for it. Others manage that well enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000046
    m_Localized: "You are doing well for yourself."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000047
    m_Localized: "While the wheel turns, perhaps. If it stops, they come to me first, not the reeve."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000048
    m_Localized: "Are you angry with them?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000049
    m_Localized: "I was. Anger spends strength, and I have little to spare. I only want them not to return."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000050
    m_Localized: "You saved the grain, not yourself."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000051
    m_Localized: "I saved myself too. I knew what they would threaten. A hungry person is a captive too, only without a door."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000052
    m_Localized: "Would you say that to the captain's face?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000053
    m_Localized: "I would. He would nod and go back to his papers. I did not stay alive to quarrel in town."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000054
    m_Localized: "Easy to say after the door opened."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000055
    m_Localized: "Easy? Sit in a pantry while strange boots pass outside. Then we can speak of easy."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000056
    m_Localized: "We should look beneath the race by daylight."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000057
    m_Localized: "We should. Not now. I will take a lantern and a hook when the mill is in order. Come by in daylight if you want; I will not go down alone."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000058
    m_Localized: "What if it knocks again?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99000000000000059
    m_Localized: "Do not answer. Do not call to it or knock back. We look in the morning. Night makes filth out of ordinary things."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000001
    m_Localized: "The Miller's Papers"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000002
    m_Localized: "Someone stole Ulrik's deeds while he was captive and intends to claim the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000003
    m_Localized: "Follow the trail of the mill papers"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000004
    m_Localized: "Speak with Hedda Roun or Keld Rook for a lead."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000005
    m_Localized: "Confront Corvin Veyr"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000006
    m_Localized: "The evidence points to Corvin Veyr and Ulrik's stolen deeds."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000007
    m_Localized: "The claim is settled"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000008
    m_Localized: "The matter of Ulrik's mill has been decided."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000009
    m_Localized: "You mentioned another trouble."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000010
    m_Localized: "They took the deed chest, not the silver. Someone knew which drawer to open. Ask around—but do not make me a saint in the telling."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000011
    m_Localized: "What do you know about Ulrik's papers?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000012
    m_Localized: "I will tell you. But first, clear a widow's debt for milling. Since her husband died, she has kept a home and children going; Ulrik does not drive her away, but he is still waiting for payment. Twenty-five crowns, and she will have one month without that fear."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000013
    m_Localized: "I will clear the widow's debt. (25 crowns)"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000014
    m_Localized: "Corvin Veyr's clerk asked about Ulrik's seal and the lock before the raid."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000015
    m_Localized: "Who paid for the mill raid?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000016
    m_Localized: "Thirty crowns go to a wounded runner. Pay it, and I will tell you whose purse reached camp."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000017
    m_Localized: "Pay for the wounded runner (30 crowns)."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000018
    m_Localized: "Corvin Veyr paid through a clerk. He wanted the deed chest, not blood."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000019
    m_Localized: "We need to speak about Ulrik's mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000020
    m_Localized: "We should speak, then. Rumours usually arrive with accusations, not papers. I have papers; you have a temper. But I dislike loud scenes. They make people braver than they are."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000021
    m_Localized: "Withdraw the claim and return Ulrik's papers."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000022
    m_Localized: "Take them. Ulrik will have his papers, along with every account I might have put before him. Do not mistake it for remorse. A dispute that walks out the door almost always costs more than a mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000023
    m_Localized: "One hundred and fifty crowns will do. Keep the papers."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000024
    m_Localized: "Sensibly done. Ulrik will keep grinding, you will leave with money, and the papers will stay where they will not be torn apart in the first bad wind. No one leaves clean, but everyone leaves alive."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000025
    m_Localized: "Well? What did you want?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000026
    m_Localized: "Tell me about yourself."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000027
    m_Localized: "About me? Fine. Just spare me cheap curiosity and ask plainly."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000028
    m_Localized: "How did you become the leader?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000029
    m_Localized: "The last leader liked waving a knife and could not count. When he was gone, there were three angry men, an empty pot, and a merchant's debt. I divided the food, cleared the debt, and said no traveler gets touched without my word. We all answer for it. That was enough. People need someone who will not leave them hungry in the morning, not the scariest man."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000030
    m_Localized: "Why keep to this place?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000031
    m_Localized: "There is one road here, and the detour is three wet days through the woods. The city shut its gates, carts stopped, and the guard watches the walls. We watch the road. Bram takes payment at the pass—he is not the leader, he is the gate. My job is stopping my fools from turning a living into slaughter."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000032
    m_Localized: "What has been happening lately?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000033
    m_Localized: "The city closed and everyone needed the road at once. Yesterday a merchant asked me to take his wagons through; today a farmer sells his knife for flour. In days like these, everyone wants their share. Then it turns out someone else paid for it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000034
    m_Localized: "Who do you answer to here?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000035
    m_Localized: "Those who keep their word. Bram likes to press with his voice, but while he listens, he suits the road. The guard wants quiet at the gate, and I want them not chasing glory in the woods. Villagers are not friends, but they are not prey either. Better to keep accounts with neighbors than old blood."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000036
    m_Localized: "Do you really read?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000037
    m_Localized: "I read. I learned letters in a debtor's pit: first so I would not sign my own noose, then I acquired the taste. Accounts, court notices, old campaign books. People lie on paper no less than face to face, only slower. Useful work: read a page and you can see who is being made a fool of."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000038
    m_Localized: "I have business to discuss."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000039
    m_Localized: "Business. Go on."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000040
    m_Localized: "The raid on Ulrik's mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000041
    m_Localized: "I heard about the mill. But you do not need gossip. You need a name. Tell me why first."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000042
    m_Localized: "The person who hired you hid behind other hands. If this comes out, he will deny you. You know that yourself."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000044
    m_Localized: "You took coin for the raid. Tell me who paid."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000045
    m_Localized: "Do not take me for a fool. I took a job: fetch a chest, hurt no one. The client feared noise more than he feared us. Such people cut loose ends first with somebody else's hands. But you came to demand, not talk. The risk is mine, the gain is yours."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000046
    m_Localized: "Fine. What do you want for the risk?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000047
    m_Localized: "Thirty crowns. Not for the name—for the silence I will need to buy after you leave. Do not haggle. You chose how to speak to me."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000048
    m_Localized: "Pay 30 crowns for the information."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000049
    m_Localized: "Corvin Veyr paid through a clerk. The deed chest was named separately, as though the silver in the house did not interest him at all. And the clerk said not to touch or read the papers. That tells me enough about whose scheme this was."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000050
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000051
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000052
    m_Localized: "Who is there? If you need goods, name them. If you want a conversation, you have strange taste."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000053
    m_Localized: "Are you Erdan Vell?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000054
    m_Localized: "The name is old. The stories around it are older still. Did you come to buy something, or repeat them to me through a door?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000055
    m_Localized: "I heard your name was connected to the Red Moon."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000056
    m_Localized: "It has been connected to plague and missing cattle too. People like it when a misfortune has one name."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000057
    m_Localized: "They spoke of children selected after the Red Moon."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000058
    m_Localized: "They were not selected after the Moon. The reaction showed earlier, and the Red Moon only made it stronger... That is exactly why I do not discuss this with people carrying rumors."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000059
    m_Localized: "Then it is true."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000060
    m_Localized: "Then you can listen. That does not mean you understand what you are speaking about."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000061
    m_Localized: "Then explain it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000062
    m_Localized: "After the Red Moon, some children changed. Not outwardly. They dreamed events that later happened. They sensed people behind walls. Sometimes things reacted beside them that an ordinary person could not affect. We wanted to know why."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000063
    m_Localized: "And then you began experimenting on them."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000064
    m_Localized: "At first we observed. Then we decided observation was not enough. We tested moonlight, blood, minerals, spells. At some point the children stopped being people to us and became a way to get an answer. It was convenient. And vile."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000065
    m_Localized: "Did any of them survive?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000066
    m_Localized: "Several. Not all left as they arrived. Then one of the survivors spoke, or one of the mages was broken. Names started passing from hand to hand. Two of my colleagues have already been found dead. I do not expect it ended with them."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000067
    m_Localized: "Why do you always speak through the door?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000068
    m_Localized: "Because a door, stone, and a good lock are more useful than most of my spells now."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000069
    m_Localized: "Are you waiting for someone to come for revenge?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000070
    m_Localized: "Not waiting. Preparing. Outside, they have woods, roads, and time. I have walls, supplies, and a chance to hear steps on the stairs. It is not a life. But on the road I would be just another name on somebody's list."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000071
    m_Localized: "About magic."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000072
    m_Localized: "If you came for a lesson, you are twenty years too late. If for goods, that I can understand."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000073
    m_Localized: "How did you become a mage?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000074
    m_Localized: "I could read, count, and did not argue with people who paid for my education. I thought that was enough. Later I learned that knowledge without restraint only gives you more ways to do harm."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000075
    m_Localized: "Why do you still trade with people?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000076
    m_Localized: "Because I need food, lamp oil, and rare substances. And because trade is the only conversation where people at least pretend to hear the terms."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000077
    m_Localized: "What is happening in the village?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000078
    m_Localized: "You are looking for gossip in the wrong place. But I notice a few obvious things even from this tower."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000079
    m_Localized: "What do you think of Cadmon?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000080
    m_Localized: "Cadmon likes it when everything has a simple explanation and one person to blame. It calms people. It does not feed a hungry person."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000081
    m_Localized: "And Meyra?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000082
    m_Localized: "Meyra has good hands and a bad habit of believing what worked once. She sees a person, not a problem. Sometimes that saves them. Sometimes it keeps her from knowing what she is treating."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000083
    m_Localized: "What did the closed gates change?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000084
    m_Localized: "While the mill works, people quarrel over the price of flour. When it stops, they will quarrel over food. The guard watches the gate, bandits watch the road, and the village counts how many days its stores will last."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000085
    m_Localized: "Do you know anything about the tavern and its travelers?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000086
    m_Localized: "I do not go to the tavern. Halvar knows who drinks, lies, and cannot pay. Livio knows who is in trouble. Both call it work."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000087
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000088
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000089
    m_Localized: "Erdan's Supply"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000090
    m_Localized: "Erdan asks for six fresh camomile flowers. He cannot leave the tower and refuses to take herbs from Meyra's supplies."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000091
    m_Localized: "Gather camomile"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000092
    m_Localized: "Gather six fresh camomile flowers for Erdan."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000093
    m_Localized: "Bring camomile to Erdan"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000094
    m_Localized: "Return to Erdan's tower and give him six camomile flowers."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000095
    m_Localized: "Do you have work for me?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000096
    m_Localized: "I do. I need camomile — six fresh flowers, not dried rubbish. It grows by the water and on sunny slopes. My supply is nearly gone, and as you can see, I do not leave this tower. Bring it and I will pay."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000097
    m_Localized: "Meyra gathers herbs."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000098
    m_Localized: "For people who need to survive the night. I will not take the last pinch from her basket merely to make myself more comfortable. And do not bring her brews; I need plain camomile."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000099
    m_Localized: "All right. I will gather it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000100
    m_Localized: "Do not tear the plants out by the root. Six flowers, clean and fresh. If Meyra is already gathering nearby, leave her patch alone."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000101
    m_Localized: "Find someone else."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000102
    m_Localized: "I brought the camomile."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000103
    m_Localized: "Six. And not soaked through — unusual care. Here are thirty-five crowns. It is not generosity; it is the price of not having to open this door."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000104
    m_Localized: "I will. The trouble is, everyone who knows how to listen is trapped behind the gate."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000105
    m_Localized: "If you came for a sermon, you will not get one. If you want to speak, speak plainly."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000106
    m_Localized: "What do you do here besides hold services?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000107
    m_Localized: "The things people usually remember too late: who needs food, whose roof leaks, who has no one to bury them. Service is not words at an altar. Words are the easy part."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000108
    m_Localized: "Why did you remain in the village?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000109
    m_Localized: "Because a parish is not a building or a post. It is people whose names you know. Leaving when things grew tight and frightening would have been convenient. I do not think much of convenience."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000110
    m_Localized: "What will the closed gate bring?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000111
    m_Localized: "First people hide flour. Then they start counting their neighbours' sacks. Once it reaches that point, the guard will be of no use. Right now, who shares water and firewood matters more than who shouts loudest at the gate."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000112
    m_Localized: "What do you think of Erdan Vell?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000113
    m_Localized: "I do not demand his tower be burned, and I do not fear the word 'mage'. I see a man accustomed to treating another life as part of a calculation. That I will not accept."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000114
    m_Localized: "You condemn what you do not know."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000115
    m_Localized: "I know enough: fear remains behind his door, and people outside inherited it. He may call the rest research, error, or necessity. Pain does not change with the name."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000116
    m_Localized: "He is afraid of revenge."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000117
    m_Localized: "Let him be afraid. Fear does not make someone a monster. Nor does it erase what made him lock himself away."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000118
    m_Localized: "Do you dislike Meyra?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000119
    m_Localized: "I dislike it when someone takes hold of a person's need without restraint. But Meyra will go to the sick at night and through mud. I respect her for that, though she would surely say she has no use for my respect."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000120
    m_Localized: "People trust her."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000121
    m_Localized: "And rightly so. Trust is not a reward for never being wrong. It is knowing you will not be abandoned when things turn bad. She does not abandon people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000122
    m_Localized: "Prayer cannot cure every sickness."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000123
    m_Localized: "It cannot. I read over the dying not because I think it can replace her hands. I do it so no one leaves alone. Do not mistake comfort for medicine."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000124
    m_Localized: "What will happen to Ulrik's mill?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000125
    m_Localized: "While it stands, it is one man's misfortune. If it stops for long, the misfortune becomes everyone's. Ulrik understands that, though he used to like people remembering who they owed their bread to."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000126
    m_Localized: "What can you tell me about the tavern and its travelers?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000127
    m_Localized: "Halvar gave people a roof when the gate closed. At a time like this, that matters more than how many cups he pours. And the travelers... each waits for the road to become someone else's concern again."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000128
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000129
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000130
    m_Localized: "If you need medicine, tell me what hurts. If you want to talk, do not stand over the baskets; herbs do not dry from conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000131
    m_Localized: "How do you treat people?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000132
    m_Localized: "First I listen. Then I look at hands, eyes, breathing. Only after that do I reach for herbs. Most people want it the other way round: drink something and never ask why they were struck down."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000133
    m_Localized: "Do you gather every herb yourself?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000134
    m_Localized: "What I can, I do. But not everything that grows belongs in a brew, and not everything picked is still good. A flower left in a wet bag for a day heals little beyond someone's conscience."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000135
    m_Localized: "How did the closed gate affect you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000136
    m_Localized: "While people are well, almost not at all. Then one day three have fever, a child begins coughing, and a good brew is down to the dregs. Gates do not make people ill. They keep what could treat them from arriving in time."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000137
    m_Localized: "What is between you and Father Cadmon?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000138
    m_Localized: "He thinks I reach too often for things that can do harm. I think he waits too long for everything to become safe. The sick do not care what you call it; they need to live until morning."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000139
    m_Localized: "But treatment is a risk."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000140
    m_Localized: "It is. That is why I do not promise miracles or push a brew into every hand. Refusing to act is a risk too. Cadmon knows it; he simply finds it easier to speak of it afterwards."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000141
    m_Localized: "He still stays with people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000142
    m_Localized: "He does. When my hands are busy, he carries water, keeps the light, sits beside those I cannot save. Not everything can be cured. That does not mean it should be abandoned."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000143
    m_Localized: "What do you think of Erdan?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000144
    m_Localized: "He can see things in a body that I would miss even after sitting by a bedside all night. It is a rare skill, and dangerous when someone forgets there is a living person before them, not a problem."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000145
    m_Localized: "He locked himself away out of fear."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000146
    m_Localized: "He did. I will not pretend I do not understand that fear. But if you can help and remain behind a door, the fear still falls on those you did not come out to help."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000147
    m_Localized: "Would you ask him to treat people?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000148
    m_Localized: "I would not. Help dragged from someone always sends a bill later. I would rather do what I can. Let him decide for himself one day who he is behind that door."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000149
    m_Localized: "What have you heard about the tavern?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000150
    m_Localized: "It is cramped and loud, and everyone pretends to know when the gate will open. Halvar feeds the travelers while he can. Livio is already watching who will decide to sell their last possession first."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000151
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000152
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000153
    m_Localized: "If you came for meat, you are late; it has all been taken. If you are heading into the woods, watch your step and listen. That is usually enough to come back."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000154
    m_Localized: "Have you hunted for long?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000155
    m_Localized: "Long enough not to call the forest mine. A beast tolerates a person while he is quiet, not greedy, and knows when to leave. People are worse at that."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000156
    m_Localized: "What is happening in the forest?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000157
    m_Localized: "There is less game by the road. More smoke, fresh stumps, and boot prints. The deer have gone deeper, and the birds are quiet by the old path. The forest is not afraid. It simply knows where it should not be."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000158
    m_Localized: "Why do you not drive the bandits off yourself?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000159
    m_Localized: "One hunter can take down a sentry. The camp will send others after that. I bring in food; I do not start a war the village will have to eat through with its stores."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000160
    m_Localized: "Bandits are not prey to you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000161
    m_Localized: "Prey does not set a watch or come to a house for revenge. With a wolf it is simpler: it is hungry, and so are you. With people, first learn what they want. Only then reach for the bow."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000162
    m_Localized: "How do the closed gates change hunting?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000163
    m_Localized: "There will be more people in the forest. Some will go for meat; others for someone else's meat. When food is scarce, there are many tracks and less game. I take only what I can carry and keep."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000164
    m_Localized: "What do you make of Meyra?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000165
    m_Localized: "She knows which part of a beast to dry and which to throw away. And she does not mind listening when I tell her where the water is foul or the tracks look sick. A sensible person does not pretend to know everything."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000166
    m_Localized: "What will become of Ulrik's mill?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000167
    m_Localized: "Hunting will not save the village without flour. Meat runs out quickly when everyone decides they deserve more. Ulrik understands that. If only he understood that bread does not make him more important than everyone else, he would be worth his price."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000168
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000169
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000170
    m_Localized: "Tell me what broke first. When someone starts from far away, it usually turns out he struck a stone and blames the iron."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000171
    m_Localized: "Have you always been a blacksmith?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000172
    m_Localized: "No. First I carried coal and worked the bellows for an old master. Then he let me hold the tongs, because his hands had begun to shake. Hammers did not make me a smith. People did, when they brought what they had managed to ruin."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000173
    m_Localized: "What can a weapon tell you about its owner?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000174
    m_Localized: "Less the weapon than how it is cared for. A clean blade can belong to a coward or a hero. But a grip wrapped in a strip of old shirt says someone cannot afford a new one right now."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000175
    m_Localized: "Do you pity people like that?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000176
    m_Localized: "Pity does not mend iron. If I can, I make the thing last another season. Then they decide whether the money goes on a grip, boots, or food."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000177
    m_Localized: "What if someone brings a weapon meant for a bad deed?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000178
    m_Localized: "I am no judge, but I am not blind. If someone asks me to make a knife better for fighting a neighbour, I send him away to cool down. If he comes back calm, we talk work. If not, he finds another smith."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000179
    m_Localized: "How have the closed gates affected the forge?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000180
    m_Localized: "At first everyone thought they would buy less steel. It went the other way: nothing new comes in, so they bring the old things to mend. Nails are straightened twice, axes honed down to a narrow tooth. Worse than a lack of iron is a lack of fuel for the forge. Without heat, every blank is only a piece of worry."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000181
    m_Localized: "What do you think of the city guard?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000182
    m_Localized: "I see their steel more often than their faces. They bring cracked shields, buckles, scabbards, and every time say it is urgent. That is their work. Mine is not to guess whom they failed to protect; it is to make sure a fastening does not fail next time."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000183
    m_Localized: "What do you make of Ulrik's mill trouble?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000184
    m_Localized: "Badly. Not because Ulrik is a saint; he haggles over every bracket. But the mill feeds people who never argued with him. When a property dispute is carried through hunger, it is no longer a dispute."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000185
    m_Localized: "Do you often work with Meyra?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000186
    m_Localized: "Sometimes. She needs clean needles, hooks, and pots that do not leak. She pays on time and does not ask for the impossible. For that, I am willing to hear about herbs, even if half their names sound like a joke."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000187
    m_Localized: "What can I buy from you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000188
    m_Localized: "Things that will not fail straight away. Time will speak for the rest. Look over the goods yourself; I will not scorn them before a sale or praise them after one."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000189
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000190
    m_Localized: "Nothing else."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000191
    m_Localized: "If you are looking for someone, ask plainly. These days people do not open even their own door to just anyone."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000192
    m_Localized: "What do you do?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000193
    m_Localized: "Whatever is most needed by evening: I carry water, help with food, watch a house while its owners are busy. The work has no fine name, but everyone notices it when there is no one left to do it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000194
    m_Localized: "How is the village holding up?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000195
    m_Localized: "Unevenly. By day everyone keeps busy and pretends the old order remains. By evening they count stores, recall old resentments, and wonder who will leave first if the gates open."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000196
    m_Localized: "Are they afraid?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000197
    m_Localized: "Of course. But fear does not always shout. Sometimes someone asks for a pot back today, though they never hurried before. Or leaves a door unlatched so they can hear the street."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000198
    m_Localized: "And are many angry?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000199
    m_Localized: "The angry ones are those who think someone else is to blame for their empty pantry. It is best not to argue about fairness with them on an empty stomach."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000200
    m_Localized: "What changed after the gates were closed?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000201
    m_Localized: "People stopped putting little things off. Those who meant to mend a roof do it now. Those who owed an apology do it too. As if finishing every loose end will open the gates sooner. It will not, of course. But it keeps their hands busy."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000202
    m_Localized: "What have you heard at the tavern?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000203
    m_Localized: "Every bit of news there grows louder than it was in the street. Halvar is holding on, not turning travelers out while he can still feed them. Livio already knows fear by what a person is willing to pawn."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000204
    m_Localized: "What do you think of Garven?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000205
    m_Localized: "He speaks sharply, but if a neighbour's lock cracks, he does not first send them looking for coin. He has his own measure of kindness: do the work honestly and do not remind them of it later."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000206
    m_Localized: "What can you tell me about Ulrik?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000207
    m_Localized: "He is used to his work being in plain sight: the wheel's noise, the sacks, the queue. Now he has to ask for help, and you hear it in every word. It is not easy for everyone to stop being the one in charge."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000208
    m_Localized: "What do you make of Meyra?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000209
    m_Localized: "She cannot soothe with words, but she comes with what can help. People do not always like that; they first want to hear that everything will be fine. She asks where it hurts."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000210
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000211
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000212
    m_Localized: "If you came for boots, first tell me where you are going. The same leather will not do for the square and the woods. If you only need to wait out the rain, there is the awning."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000213
    m_Localized: "What do you trade in?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000214
    m_Localized: "Footwear, hats, belts. Things people remember only when they begin to chafe, freeze, or lose their purse. Good clothing does not make a person richer. It keeps trouble from noticing them too early."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000215
    m_Localized: "Why do you care so much about footwear?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000216
    m_Localized: "Because the road takes your feet first. Rub a heel raw and you slow down. Soak your boots and you freeze. Tear a sole and you watch the ground instead of the way ahead. Then people wonder how a small thing ruined a big plan."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000217
    m_Localized: "Have you travelled much yourself?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000218
    m_Localized: "Enough. Trade taught me that words can be cheaper than a wagon, but you still have to carry the goods yourself. Now I can tell whose feet ache by the way they approach a stall."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000219
    m_Localized: "Not everyone can pay for good boots."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000220
    m_Localized: "I know. I do not offer an expensive pair to someone who needs a patch until spring. A strap can be replaced, a sole mended. Not everything must be bought new, even if that would profit the seller."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000221
    m_Localized: "How have the closed gates affected trade?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000222
    m_Localized: "Caravans do not arrive, and people look at goods not to choose but to judge whether they will last the season. Sizes run out in no order, and leather does not appear by wishing. I have to say no more often than I like."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000223
    m_Localized: "What is happening with the travelers at the tavern?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000224
    m_Localized: "They still stand by the door as if someone will shout that the road is clear any moment. One bought a hat for the wind and wears it indoors, not from cold but so he need not think about how long he will wait. People on the road do not know how to stand still."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000225
    m_Localized: "Have you raised your prices?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000226
    m_Localized: "On what has become dearer to me, yes. Not on what someone urgently needs. You can profit from the cold, but then that cold will stand at your own door. Livio would likely say that is no way to count. Everyone has their own reckoning."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000227
    m_Localized: "What do you think of Garven?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000228
    m_Localized: "Garven curses a bad buckle as if it were made to spite him. Then he takes a hammer and fixes it. He is easy to work with: if a strap will not hold, he says so plainly instead of pretending the buyer is at fault."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000229
    m_Localized: "What do you make of Meyra?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000230
    m_Localized: "I stitch straps for her bags and sheaths for glass vials. She knows dirty hands can be worse than a bad herb. With her, you can speak of work instead of miracles."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000231
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000232
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000233
    m_Localized: "If you need a door, tell me where the opening is. If you need advice, say that too. I do not like guessing what someone wants to build out of another person's words."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000234
    m_Localized: "What do you do?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000235
    m_Localized: "Roofs, doors, carts, fences. All the things no one looks at while they hold. Then something warps, and they remember Rogan at once. That is the proper order."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000236
    m_Localized: "What matters most in carpentry?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000237
    m_Localized: "Not rushing when the wood is still damp. A board looks straight on the outside, then it warps and takes the whole job with it. People like to cut time short. Wood always collects for it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000238
    m_Localized: "Can wood deceive you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000239
    m_Localized: "It does not deceive. It speaks quietly at first: through a knot, a crack, a damp edge. If you do not listen, it answers later with a door that will not close in frost."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000240
    m_Localized: "Does every job need to be redone?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000241
    m_Localized: "Some do. Better to remake one beam than prop up a whole roof later. That is obvious in work. With people, for some reason, they wait until it collapses."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000242
    m_Localized: "What have the closed gates changed in your work?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000243
    m_Localized: "More orders, less material. People mend shutters, brace gates, move firewood closer to the house. Not because wood protects from everything. When all around is uncertain, they want at least their own things not to creak."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000244
    m_Localized: "What is happening in the forest now?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000245
    m_Localized: "I no longer go far for good timber. There are too many unfamiliar tracks by the road, and dead wood can be found here. Harn says the forest tells you where a person is not wanted. I believe him. I do not want to learn how loudly it can say it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000246
    m_Localized: "Do you work with Garven?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000247
    m_Localized: "All the time. A good door without hinges is boards, and a good fence without brackets is asking the wind not to blow. Garven knows how to make iron simple. That is a rare gift."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000248
    m_Localized: "What do you think of Harn?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000249
    m_Localized: "He speaks little, but he does not promise the forest to people who will not return from it. For a man in his work, that matters more than pleasant words."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000250
    m_Localized: "Does Meyra order anything from you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000251
    m_Localized: "Boxes for drying herbs and shelves to keep things off the floor. She asks how much a board will bear before she puts a jar on it. That makes for easy work."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000252
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000253
    m_Localized: "That is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000254
    m_Localized: "If you came to look at the soil, look. Just do not ask why it keeps quiet. The soil answers late."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000255
    m_Localized: "Do you work in the fields?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000256
    m_Localized: "I do. I sow, weed, mend ditches, see what has come up and what must be sown again. There is no spare work in a field: leave it until tomorrow, and tomorrow it takes twice as long."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000257
    m_Localized: "What is hardest about fieldwork?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000258
    m_Localized: "Not mistaking patience for idleness. Sometimes you wait for the ground to take the water. Sometimes you get into the mud now, or the water takes everything. From outside, it looks the same: standing and watching."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000259
    m_Localized: "Is a harvest always a gamble?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000260
    m_Localized: "No. A gamble is sowing whatever comes to hand and hoping for luck. We can prepare the ground, save seed, pull weeds in time. The rest is not ours. But that is enough not to sit idle."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000261
    m_Localized: "So the weather decides everything?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000262
    m_Localized: "The weather decides much. But a bad ditch, a blunt hoe, and a person who arrives late decide no less. It is convenient to blame the sky for everything. The soil does not accept that."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000263
    m_Localized: "How have the closed gates changed the work?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000264
    m_Localized: "Now we count not only sacks, but seeds. If there is nothing to sow in spring, there is nothing to mill in autumn. People see food in the granary. I see it still in the handful that must not be eaten now."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000265
    m_Localized: "What does Ulrik's mill mean for the fields?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000266
    m_Localized: "Without it, grain is only heavy sacks. Ulrik turns our work into bread, and people forgave him much for that. But when his trouble became the village's trouble, everyone had to remember: the mill does not stand apart from the fields."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000267
    m_Localized: "Do you speak with Harn often?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000268
    m_Localized: "When animals get into the crops, often. He does not promise to drive off every one, but he explains where to put rattles and when not to leave a field unattended. His mind works more quietly than most."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000269
    m_Localized: "Does Meyra come to your fields?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000270
    m_Localized: "She takes what does not go in a sack: roots, leaves, flowers along the field's edge. But first she asks what I used on the ground and where it is sick. It is good when someone knows the cost of what they gather."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000271
    m_Localized: "And Father Cadmon?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000272
    m_Localized: "He comes when hands are scarce at sowing time. He does not pretend to work better than us: he carries water, clears stones, listens. That helps a field more than proper words."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000273
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000274
    m_Localized: "I should go. I do not want to keep you."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000275
    m_Localized: "If you brought laundry, put it over there. If you brought conversation, stand here—just do not tread on the wet things."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000276
    m_Localized: "Do you wash and mend clothes here?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000277
    m_Localized: "I wash, mend, and lift stains. I keep a tub, soap, a needle, and other people's patience. It is not heroic work, but afterward people go back among others as if nothing happened to them."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000278
    m_Localized: "Can you really tell much from clothes?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000279
    m_Localized: "A great deal. But not everything you can see should be repeated. Look at a shirt: soot ground into the elbow, burrs at the hem, a collar rubbed by a strap. Someone worked, went through brush, carried a load. Where and why is no business of mine."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000280
    m_Localized: "So you judge people by appearances after all?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000281
    m_Localized: "No. I would be judging if I decided whether someone was good or bad. Laundry tells me what was done to it. A person is another matter."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000282
    m_Localized: "Do people really bring their secrets to you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000283
    m_Localized: "Not secrets. Dirt, yes. A secret usually lives not in the cloth, but in someone starting to explain when nobody asked."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000284
    m_Localized: "What have the closed gates changed for you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000285
    m_Localized: "The road used to bring dust, blood, wine, and ink. Now people mend old things before they wear anything new, and think twice before spending a piece of soap on a collar. Trouble does not always arrive shouting. Sometimes it just makes cloth thinner."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000286
    m_Localized: "Does Halvar send his laundry to you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000287
    m_Localized: "He does. And he knows I do not sort through who slept in which room. There is less bedding now, and more worry in it. An empty room leaves a mark too—especially on an innkeeper."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000288
    m_Localized: "What does Ulrik's mill mean to you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000289
    m_Localized: "When the wheel stopped, every basket suddenly held less certainty. Flour washes out easily. It is worse when people start dividing the last sack as if it will never be replaced."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000290
    m_Localized: "Does Meyra ever ask you for help?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000291
    m_Localized: "She asks for old clean linen for bandages and sometimes teaches me how to boil it so it will not harm the wounded. She is not gentle. But when blood is involved, her hands do more good than many kind words."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000292
    m_Localized: "How do you see the guard?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000293
    m_Localized: "Their boots dirty the floor like anyone else's. But people watch them more closely: when a guard walks past someone else's trouble, everyone notices. And when one helps, people more often remember how long they waited."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000294
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000295
    m_Localized: "Thank you. I should go."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000296
    m_Localized: "Not now."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000297
    m_Localized: "If you can name the matter in two sentences, do so. If not, sit down and begin with what you want."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000298
    m_Localized: "What do you do in the village?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000299
    m_Localized: "I buy stock when someone has a surplus, lend when someone has a shortfall, and bring people together when they need to sell one another what they do not have time for. Does it sound ugly? Work rarely looks beautiful when you only look at the sums."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000300
    m_Localized: "Do you always think about debts?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000301
    m_Localized: "Debt is not a mark of shame. It is a promise that today's hardship will not be the last word. The trouble is not borrowing. It is convincing yourself there are no terms and that someone else will pay anyway."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000302
    m_Localized: "Do you count people as numbers?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000303
    m_Localized: "If I did, I would not lend. A number does not ask for time, bury kin, or lie to itself from shame. But without numbers I cannot tell where help becomes the habit of living at another's expense."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000304
    m_Localized: "And when are debts forgiven?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000305
    m_Localized: "When collecting breaks both sides. A poor man without a roof will return nothing; a neighbour helped once may stand again and return more than money. Mercy without memory is foolishness. Calculation without it is too."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000306
    m_Localized: "How have the closed gates changed your work?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000307
    m_Localized: "The circle has narrowed. Goods do not arrive, money lies still, and people fear spending even on what they need. On days like these, those who promise everyone their old life back for one simple signature are especially dangerous."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000308
    m_Localized: "Why stay in this village?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000309
    m_Localized: "There is water, fields, skilled work, and a road—when it is not closed. People call places like this poor until they see how much labour passes through one yard. I prefer to invest where the result can be seen without a map."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000310
    m_Localized: "What do you think of Ulrik?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000311
    m_Localized: "He is a good miller: he knows the wheel, the water, and the grain. That is no small thing. But a business also needs dates, papers, and agreements, and he treats them as tiresome details. Men like that remember the law when it is already at the door."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000312
    m_Localized: "How do you regard Meyra?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000313
    m_Localized: "She sells not hope, but what she knows how to do. She is sometimes wrong, but she does not hide it behind fine words. Useful in a deal. For friendship, I cannot say."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000314
    m_Localized: "Do you trust the guard?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000315
    m_Localized: "You entrust the guard with what cannot be settled between yourselves. But waiting for them instead of making your own decision is an expensive habit. They come when they can; the village still pays the price of delay."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000316
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000317
    m_Localized: "That is enough for today."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000318
    m_Localized: "I need to think."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000319
    m_Localized: "Return Ulrik's documents"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000320
    m_Localized: "The papers were returned to their rightful owner. The mill remains Ulrik's."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000321
    m_Localized: "Accept Corvin's deal"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000322
    m_Localized: "The dispute over the mill has been settled by a deal. Corvin keeps the documents."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000323
    m_Localized: "Do you have the papers?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000324
    m_Localized: "I do. Locked in a drawer, where they should have been from the start. Strange to be glad about a scrap with a seal, but now that the water is turning the wheel, I can think about flour instead of who will arrive with another man's signature."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000325
    m_Localized: "What will happen to the mill now?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000326
    m_Localized: "The wheel is turning. That is the main thing for now. But the papers are still not with me. Corvin says the agreement settles it; I have seen agreements like that reopen when someone needs to press another person. I will keep the accounts straight and give him no excuse."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000327
    m_Localized: "How have the fields weathered the trouble at the mill?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000328
    m_Localized: "People have stopped hiding grain in their chests. They know they can take it over and have it ground. One paper has not added any bread, but without it everyone would have started saving only their own sack."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000329
    m_Localized: "What do people say about the deal with Corvin?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000330
    m_Localized: "They speak quietly. The mill is working, and everyone is glad of that. But now, before bringing grain, a person wonders who they are really promising their labour to. A thought like that does not dry out a field, but it makes the hands heavier."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000331
    m_Localized: "Has it grown calmer since the papers were returned?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000332
    m_Localized: "Calmer. People bring laundry to the river again and argue over stains instead of who will get the last sack of flour. I know calm does not always mean justice. But at least people here have stopped waiting for the next blow."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000333
    m_Localized: "What do people think of Corvin's deal?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000334
    m_Localized: "Everyone thinks their own thoughts and pretends to know nothing. Ulrik holds himself together, Corvin is polite, the mill makes its noise. But the clothes tell it: people have begun hiding their purses under their shirts more often. They do not believe the matter is over."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000335
    m_Localized: "Did you give up the mill?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000336
    m_Localized: "I gave up a paper acquired improperly. Do not mistake that for remorse: I simply will not hold property on such a foundation. Ulrik has been given a chance. What he does with it is his own account."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000337
    m_Localized: "Are you satisfied with the deal?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000338
    m_Localized: "Satisfied is the wrong word. We found a price at which you stopped pursuing the matter and Ulrik kept his work. The papers will stay with me until the city opens; then I will decide how to formalise everything without needless noise. For the village, the wheel turning matters more just now."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000339
    m_Localized: "Has the tavern always been this full?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000340
    m_Localized: "No. A full tavern is when people arrive in the evening, eat, kick up dust in the morning, and leave. Now they count coppers, ask for another night on credit, and listen to the door as if the road will open behind it. A guest who does not know when they leave becomes almost a neighbour."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000341
    m_Localized: "And you will not turn anyone out?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000342
    m_Localized: "Not while I can put a bowl before them. But pity has to be counted too: give everything away today, and tomorrow everyone behind this counter will be cold. So I cut the bread thinner and write down every debt. Nothing noble about it. It is simply how a house holds together longer."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000343
    m_Localized: "How have the closed gates changed your work?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000344
    m_Localized: "First the fresh barrels stopped coming, then salt, then people stopped ordering a second mug. Now the soup is thick not from meat, but because I have learned not to throw away anything edible. The gates did not close a road. They closed tomorrow's delivery."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000345
    m_Localized: "So you work on credit?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000346
    m_Localized: "Sometimes. But I do not let a person forget it is a debt. Tomorrow they may need not a mug, but a place by the hearth. Better to speak plainly now than watch them hide their eyes later."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000347
    m_Localized: "Who are the people staying here?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000348
    m_Localized: "The same sort as anywhere: one waits for good news, another for a convenient chance. Marta keeps her things packed as if departure were set for dawn. Edric argues with rumours until he tires himself out. Runa watches more than she speaks. And Tarek… Tarek pays on time and does his best not to be remembered."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000349
    m_Localized: "Which of them worries you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000350
    m_Localized: "The one certain trouble only happens to other people. That person is first to raise an alarm and last to fetch a bucket when the roof catches fire. The others at least understand they are stuck together."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000351
    m_Localized: "Does Livio help you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000352
    m_Localized: "He can find the price of a thing when its owner is ready to give it away for a bowl of stew. Sometimes that saves a person; sometimes it leaves them without their last possession. I do not call it help, but Livio does not meddle with my barrels and he pays for his table. That is already something."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000353
    m_Localized: "Do you trust him?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000354
    m_Localized: "I trust him to count. I check everything else myself. It is no insult; with people in his trade, that keeps both them and you calmer."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000355
    m_Localized: "Have you known Ulrik long?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000356
    m_Localized: "A long while. He used to come after milling, sit by the wall, and listen to everyone else first. Then he ordered food for the workers, not only for himself. Ulrik is stubborn and no friend to paperwork, but he remembers whose sack he held up and who needs flour first. For a miller, that matters more than fine speech."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000357
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000358
    m_Localized: "That is enough for today."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000359
    m_Localized: "If you want to talk, talk to me. Leave my brother alone."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000360
    m_Localized: "Why does Edric not answer?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000361
    m_Localized: "He can speak. He simply will not. Not with strangers, certainly. Do not take it personally: this is how he holds himself together when there are too many people and questions around him. I am his sister, Runa."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000362
    m_Localized: "Did something happen to him?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000363
    m_Localized: "To both of us. They took us as children, told our parents they would examine a fever after the Red Moon. In the records, we were called sensitive. The mages tested what its light did to us and called it treatment. After one such night, Edric asked them to stop. They wrote: 'subject is uncooperative.' He did not ask again."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000364
    m_Localized: "Who did it?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000365
    m_Localized: "People in clean sleeves. Some called the children by numbers, others by names. Most vanished when the truth came out. But one name remained in the papers and in the stories of those who survived: Erdan Vell."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000366
    m_Localized: "Are you looking for Erdan Vell?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000367
    m_Localized: "We are. We followed old letters and scraps of other people's words until we heard of a mage in a tower. I do not know whether it is truly him. But if it is Erdan, he cannot say he does not remember us: he had our names."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000368
    m_Localized: "What will you do if you find him?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000369
    m_Localized: "I will not promise a pretty answer. Edric wants to look him in the face. I want him to name what he did in his own words, not call it 'research' or 'necessity.' And after that… we will learn which of us can still stop."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000370
    m_Localized: "What did the Red Moon do to you?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000371
    m_Localized: "For the mages, it was an explanation. For us, heat beneath the skin, sleeplessness, and dreams after which you woke without knowing the room. Sometimes glass cracked from fear; sometimes we heard other voices. They awaited those days like a feast."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000372
    m_Localized: "Why were you chosen?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000373
    m_Localized: "Because we reacted. For other children, the Moon was only a red point above the roof. We developed a fever. The mages said it was rare, a chance to understand something important. Rare is a useful word when you do not want to say 'child.'"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000374
    m_Localized: "Why did you stay when the gates closed?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000375
    m_Localized: "Because we were already here. And because Edric will not leave before he checks the tower. I will not drag him through a closed gate like a sack. We waited too long to turn away at the threshold."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000376
    m_Localized: "What if Erdan is not here?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000377
    m_Localized: "Then we will go on. This is not the first door that has closed before us. But I still hope he is here. Hope is not always a good feeling; sometimes it simply keeps you from lying down and giving up the search."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000378
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000379
    m_Localized: "I should go."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000380
    m_Localized: "If you have an item to sell, show it to me. If you have a conversation, speak plainly. Time has a price too."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000381
    m_Localized: "What do you do?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000382
    m_Localized: "I buy what one person no longer needs or cannot carry, and find someone who can use it. A tool, a jewel, a travel thing: each has a price, but it changes with place, time, and who can afford to wait. My trade is not confusing an item's price with its owner's panic."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000383
    m_Localized: "But you still profit from another person's need."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000384
    m_Localized: "Sometimes even a fair price sounds insulting when someone needs coin before evening. I did not create their need, but I can choose how much to exploit it. A warm cloak, a working knife, a person's last boots: I do not pay coppers for such things. A deal made too cheaply often comes back to you as someone else's misery."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000385
    m_Localized: "How have the closed gates changed your business?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000386
    m_Localized: "The market has become small and nervous. Goods exist, but there is no buyer beyond the gate. People hide coins as if they could warm themselves with them; meanwhile any belt or pot that cannot be replaced suddenly costs more than silver. Now I count not only an item's worth, but whether we can find another in a month."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000387
    m_Localized: "Who loses most from that?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000388
    m_Localized: "The person who needs money today and the item tomorrow. The rich can wait; the poor sell what they will later need to work. That is why, in a closed city, gold is not the costliest thing. Time is."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000389
    m_Localized: "Why do you sit in the tavern?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000390
    m_Localized: "Because you hear what is happening here before you do in the square. A person does not bring an item to sell in silence: first they complain about the road, a debt, a broken lock. A tavern is a market before the item reaches the table. I listen, but I do not enter another person's conversation uninvited."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000391
    m_Localized: "Does Halvar allow that?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000392
    m_Localized: "Halvar lets me use a table while I do not turn his house into a trap for the desperate. He keeps his own accounts: bowls, firewood, people under the roof. I keep mine: objects and deadlines. We do not share ledgers, and that is why we get along better than many business partners."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000393
    m_Localized: "How did you become a buyer?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000394
    m_Localized: "At first I ran between shops with other people's parcels and counted what the owner lost to every middleman. Then I learned to tell good steel from polished junk, and to listen when someone called their own possession worthless. This trade rarely begins with a grand deal. Usually, it begins when someone cheats you once."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000395
    m_Localized: "Why keep doing such work?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000396
    m_Localized: "Because a thing lying unused with one person can feed another or carry them home. Money is not the purpose; it is a way not to argue for hours over who owes whom. Of course people can make dirt of it. But dirt does not vanish when you stop noticing what it sticks to."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000397
    m_Localized: "Do you know Corvin Veyr?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000398
    m_Localized: "We know each other's names. That is enough. Corvin works in promises: he gives a person time, then sees what they will pay for it. I work with what lies before me. He sees future profit; I see a present price. Sometimes those views meet. I would not call it friendship."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000399
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000400
    m_Localized: "That is all."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000401
    m_Localized: "Best approach horses without sudden words. They do not understand them anyway, but they remember a hand."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000402
    m_Localized: "You seem to think more about horses than guests."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000403
    m_Localized: "A guest sleeps and leaves. A horse leaves, and the guest stays with you: angry and on foot. So first I know who is lame and who did not drink enough; only then do I hear who lacks a pillow."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000404
    m_Localized: "Is that enough to make one obey?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000405
    m_Localized: "No. But shouting only makes a horse obey out of fear, and a frightened horse brings more trouble on the road. First let it know you saw the fear. Then ask it to work. It is not so different with people."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000406
    m_Localized: "What is your work besides the stalls?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000407
    m_Localized: "Stalls are half of it. Hooves, harness, water, oats, a roof against rain. Then listening to the owner: they always know why a horse will not go, until we find a strap has rubbed its shoulder. A good stablehand notices first."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000408
    m_Localized: "How have the closed gates affected the stable?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000409
    m_Localized: "People can wait and make up reasons for it. An animal cannot: it needs feed today. There are fewer travellers, but more horses left behind because those stranded do not want to abandon them on the road. There is room. Oats have to be counted."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000410
    m_Localized: "Will the feed last?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000411
    m_Localized: "If nobody starts feeding their colt like a lord, it will last a while. Halvar arranged hay with the farmers; I set the horses on rations. It is not pretty, but it is fair: one full horse is not worth three hungry ones."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000412
    m_Localized: "Have you worked on the road long?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000413
    m_Localized: "Since I was small. First I carried water into another man's yard for a bowl of stew. Then an old stablehand gave me a brush and told me not to get underfoot. A year later he trusted me with a mare that had a temper. I thought: if she did not throw me, I might last here."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000414
    m_Localized: "Do you not want to leave yourself?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000415
    m_Localized: "I did, until I rode with a caravan. The road is fine when you are its guest. When you have four animals, wet bundles, and an owner who cannot read the sky behind you, you soon appreciate a dry stable. I have nothing against travel. I just know its price."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000416
    m_Localized: "You see the guests before anyone else. What do you make of them?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000417
    m_Localized: "A horse tells you plenty. Marta keeps everything ready: her packs are tied twice over, as if the gates will open any moment. Runa does not take the reins herself, but watches her brother breathe when it gets loud. Livio asks where people came from as if he is only making conversation. Everyone has their own way of waiting."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000418
    m_Localized: "Are you afraid of the forest road?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000419
    m_Localized: "I am afraid when there is reason. Fear on the road helps if it does not make you foolish: do not enter darkness, do not run a horse over stones, do not put yourself between strangers and their quarrel. The rest is luck and how well you prepared."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000420
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000421
    m_Localized: "I will not keep you."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000422
    m_Localized: "If you want to talk, talk. Just do not touch my bag: I spent too long learning not to leave my things unwatched."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000423
    m_Localized: "Have you waited long for the gates to open?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000424
    m_Localized: "Long enough to stop asking the guard every morning. I came through this village for two nights, and now I know how Halvar counts firewood and when Orren takes the horses to water. Not the knowledge one sets out to gain."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000425
    m_Localized: "Do you have to get beyond the gates?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000426
    m_Localized: "I do. I left work elsewhere and promised to return by a date. While I am here, other people's letters and accounts lie unanswered. Nothing heroic. People simply dislike having their important words stuck in someone else's bag."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000427
    m_Localized: "You work with letters and accounts?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000428
    m_Localized: "I copy contracts, letters, and sometimes keep accounts for those with no time or skill for it. On paper, people are usually braver: they promise more than they would say to a face. My work is making sure it is possible to see later who promised what."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000429
    m_Localized: "Why are your things always packed?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000430
    m_Localized: "Because packing when it is already time to leave is a fine way to forget what matters. I check straps in the evening, not at dawn. If the gates open suddenly, I will not have to choose between my place in a caravan and my ink bottle."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000431
    m_Localized: "Do you always expect the worst?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000432
    m_Localized: "I account for plans changing. That is different. Best not call for the worst ahead of time; it knows the road without an invitation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000433
    m_Localized: "What have the closed gates done to people?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000434
    m_Localized: "At first everyone was angry. Then they began speaking more quietly and listening to the door more often. Some fear losing money; some fear bad news is already waiting at home. A delay is not simply another day. It is a day you cannot tell anyone about."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000435
    m_Localized: "Do you write down everything you hear?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000436
    m_Localized: "No. Another person's worry is not a draft for my work. I notice when someone needs to speak and when it is better to leave them alone. Those are different skills. I learned the second one first."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000437
    m_Localized: "How are you finding life in the tavern?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000438
    m_Localized: "Crowded, noisy, but honest. Halvar does not promise everyone comfort, but in the morning there is still a fire and stew. Runa stays close to her brother. Livio stays close to other people's things. I keep a place by the wall so no one sits on my papers. Everyone manages as they can."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000439
    m_Localized: "Can you read something for me?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000440
    m_Localized: "I can, if it is yours and you know why you are listening. But do not ask me to read another person's letter over their shoulder. Paper can keep boundaries too."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000441
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000442
    m_Localized: "I should go."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000443
    m_Localized: "If a strap, lock, or sheath has broken, show me. If you only want to talk, sit down. I do not bite."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000444
    m_Localized: "You try not to draw attention."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000445
    m_Localized: "I try not to be in the way. Different thing. Pay on time, stay out of another person's quarrel, return a tool whole, and people remember you when they need you. Enough for me."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000446
    m_Localized: "You do not like people?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000447
    m_Localized: "I do. I have simply seen places where one careless word makes a person known, and then they are sold that word back for a week. I do not like that trade."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000448
    m_Localized: "How do you earn your living?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000449
    m_Localized: "I mend what people are sorry to throw away: buckles, sheaths, door hinges, straps, travel pots. Small work, but it reminds you at the right time that not everything useful looks expensive."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000450
    m_Localized: "Where did you learn it?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000451
    m_Localized: "From a master who said: first find why a thing broke, then charge for mending it. Otherwise tomorrow they bring you the same thing, only angrier. I did not stay with him long, but I kept that lesson."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000452
    m_Localized: "Do the closed gates trouble you much?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000453
    m_Localized: "They trouble everyone, only differently. I used to mend things on the road and move on. Now something breaks here, and there is nowhere to replace it. More work, less metal. That is the arithmetic of it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000454
    m_Localized: "Do you take coin for repairs now?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000455
    m_Localized: "If someone can pay, I take it. If not, I ask what the thing is for. For a working knife or harness strap, we can sometimes make an arrangement. Not generosity: without them, a person soon becomes trouble to themselves and everyone else."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000456
    m_Localized: "What do you think of the people in the tavern?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000457
    m_Localized: "Each holds to their own. Marta to order. Runa to her brother. Halvar to a house that must not come apart. Livio to the price of things. Nothing unusual. It is simply all visible here because nobody can leave yet."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000458
    m_Localized: "Have you travelled the roads much?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000459
    m_Localized: "Enough not to call the road freedom. It only trades one worry for another: where to sleep, whom to trust, how not to soak your tools. But the road is honest in one way: if you did the work well, it shows at once."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000460
    m_Localized: "And the forest road?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000461
    m_Localized: "I walk where people walk and do not seek shortcuts through another person's ground. I have heard the same of bandits as everyone. But when a road goes empty, tracks lie before rumours do. I watch them more closely."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000462
    m_Localized: "Return to the conversation."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000463
    m_Localized: "Take care."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000464
    m_Localized: "Oswin Marlow asked me to see how you were. He says he has had no word from you in a long while."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000465
    m_Localized: "Oswin worries as if he has a bell where his heart should be. Tell him this: I am alive, working, and doing well. I have even taken on an apprentice — in two years she has learned to hold the tongs and argue about iron. Oswin and I have not seen each other for just as long. When the roads open, I will call on him myself. And ask why he decided I had vanished."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000466
    m_Localized: "Bring Oswin the news"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000467
    m_Localized: "Return to Oswin and deliver Garven's message."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000468
    m_Localized: "I found Garven. He is alive, doing well, and asked me to tell you that he has had an apprentice for two years now."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000469
    m_Localized: "An apprentice? So Garven has finally learned not to carry all the work by himself. That is good news. Thank you for going. When we meet, I expect he will explain why he kept quiet for two years — and I will explain why I spent that time waiting for word from him."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000470
    m_Localized: "Speak with Elina"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000471
    m_Localized: "Halvar says Elina is by the river. Find her and make sure she is all right."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000472
    m_Localized: "Speak with Elina at the tavern"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000473
    m_Localized: "Elina has gone back to the tavern. Continue the conversation there."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000474
    m_Localized: "Yes?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000475
    m_Localized: "What do you like about the river?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000476
    m_Localized: "It never asks whether I have washed the cups or counted the linen. I can sit here for ten minutes, listen to the water, and come back to the tavern without wanting to bite anyone. That is already plenty."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000477
    m_Localized: "The river does not hold grudges. Useful quality."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000478
    m_Localized: "The captain of the guard asked me to see whether you are all right."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000479
    m_Localized: "Of course he did. He notices a loose buckle three streets away, but will stand at our door and forget why he came. Tell him I am well. Better yet, do not tell him anything yet. I will be at the tavern; he can hear it from me when he finds the courage."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000480
    m_Localized: "Your father is worried. He says you often come here."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000481
    m_Localized: "Father worries when I am two steps from the door. He is not wrong, only exhausting. Since you have spoken with him, tell him I will come back before the stew burns. Then meet me at the tavern if you still want answers."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000482
    m_Localized: "Is it hard to be back at the tavern?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000483
    m_Localized: "Hard is too grand a word. There are cups to dry, travelers to feed, and Father pretending he did not save the stool beside him for me. Work puts things in order. Sometimes that is enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000484
    m_Localized: "You seem to have learned the rhythm of this place."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000485
    m_Localized: "Are you angry with the captain?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000486
    m_Localized: "No. Anger would be easier. He is decent, and so careful not to overstep that he sometimes steps right out of his own life. I do not need a man to watch me from a gate. I need him to speak plainly."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000487
    m_Localized: "Fair enough."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000488
    m_Localized: "Let us talk about something else."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000489
    m_Localized: "I am looking for Elina. Is she by the river?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000490
    m_Localized: "She is. Goes there when this room feels too close. If the captain sent you, do not make it sound like an inspection. She will hear concern even if you wrap it in orders."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000491
    m_Localized: "I need to know how Elina is doing. She is Halvar's daughter — the innkeeper on the road. With the city shut, people disappear into their own worries. Find her, speak with her, and bring me the truth, not a polite answer."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000492
    m_Localized: "I will find Elina and speak with her."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000493
    m_Localized: "Thank you. She is usually by the river. You may speak with Halvar first if you wish; he knows when something is weighing on her. And do not question her like a witness."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000494
    m_Localized: "News of Elina"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000495
    m_Localized: "The captain of the city guard asks you to make sure Elina, Halvar's daughter, is safe."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000496
    m_Localized: "Speak with Elina"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000497
    m_Localized: "Elina is usually by the river. You may speak with Halvar before you go to her."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000498
    m_Localized: "It is personal, but not only that. Elina is capable; that is precisely why she does not ask for help when she should. I would rather hear she is well than spend another day imagining the worst."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000499
    m_Localized: "Do you know where I can get apples?"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99200000000000500
    m_Localized: "There is an apple tree right in front of us. You can wait for the apples to fall on their own, or give the trunk a couple of knocks — maybe a pair will come down. Just do not lay into it."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000001
    m_Localized: "Pay Ulrik's ransom"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000002
    m_Localized: "Bram Voss demands two thousand coins to release the miller."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000003
    m_Localized: "Pay the rest of Ulrik's ransom"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000004
    m_Localized: "Bram took the money and demands another five hundred coins."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000005
    m_Localized: "Ulrik is free"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000006
    m_Localized: "The ransom has been paid and the bandits have left the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000007
    m_Localized: "The mill is liberated"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000008
    m_Localized: "The guard drove the bandits from the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000009
    m_Localized: "The mill is liberated"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000010
    m_Localized: "You fought beside the guard and helped retake the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000011
    m_Localized: "The mill is liberated"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000012
    m_Localized: "The guard's reward has been received."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000013
    m_Localized: "The guard is defeated"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000014
    m_Localized: "You fought beside the bandits and helped them hold the mill."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000015
    m_Localized: "The bandits hold the mill"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000016
    m_Localized: "Varek's reward has been received."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000017
    m_Localized: "The bandits hold the mill"
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99300000000000018
    m_Localized: "The bandit camp reward has been received."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99400000000000001
    m_Localized: "I did. The bandits hold the miller. I saw where they stand and how they approach the building."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99400000000000002
    m_Localized: "Good. Lead us in and show us the best way through. We need to reach the miller before one of those dogs loses his nerve."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99400000000000003
    m_Localized: "I will. And I am not standing aside."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99400000000000004
    m_Localized: "That is what I wanted to hear. Stay with the squad and watch the flank. When we see the bandits, we cut them down fast and do not let them touch the miller."
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99500000000000001
    m_Localized: YOU DIED
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99500000000000002
    m_Localized: Press any key
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99500000000000003
    m_Localized: Trade
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99500000000000004
    m_Localized: Sell
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99500000000000005
    m_Localized: Buy
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
  - m_Id: 99500000000000006
    m_Localized: Exit
    m_Metadata: {m_Items: []}
